; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2000  /***********************************************************************************************************************
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2001   *  MISRA JUSTIFICATIONS
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2002   **********************************************************************************************************************/
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2003  /* Justification for module-specific MISRA deviations:
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2004  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2005  MD_NvM_8.9:
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2006    Reason: Query function table logically belongs to the NvM_Qry. Due to architectural decisions this table shall stay
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2007            here for now.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2008    Risk: Components including the NvM_Qry.h file could directly call queries which then interfere with the intrinsic
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2009          behavior of the component.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2010    Prevention: A code review should ensure that usage of this table is done correctly.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2011  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2012  MD_NvM_8.9_CrcHandlerTable
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2013    Reason: The array NvM_CrcHandlerTable_at stores all possible CRC handlers, the implementation simply uses the configured
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2014            CRC type as an index into the table to use the correct CRC handler.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2015            Instead of the table the CRC handler could be set within a if else if statements or similar, but the table avoids
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2016            decisions within the code, but costs a bit memory.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2017    Risk: No risk.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2018    Prevention: No prevention, component tests and reviews ensure functionality.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2019  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2020  MD_NvM_8.9_TestBuffer
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2021    Reason: To check the readability of a (redundant) NvM block, NvM uses a single byte NvM_TestBuffer_u8 - during a read and
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2022            RepairRedundantBlocks. In case the RepairRedundantBlocks feature is disabled, the buffer will only be accessed once.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2023    Risk: No risk.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2024    Prevention: No prevention, component tests and reviews ensure functionality.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2025  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2026  MD_NvM_8.9_StateTable
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2027    Reason: The state descriptor table holds the complete NvM state machine - all states. NvM_Fsm is the only function
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2028            accessing the state table since the function is the one moving the NvM from one state to the next and so on.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2029            NvM is not allowed to access the table from another sub modules and/ or functions.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2030    Risk: No risk.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2031    Prevention: No prevention, component tests and reviews ensure functionality.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2032  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2033  MD_NvM_8.9_DataIntegrity_SubmoduleUsedOnlyInOneFunction:
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2034    Reason:     The data integrity submodule uses redirections to explicit data integrity modules. Instances to it are
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2035                stored at "private" file scope.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2036    Risk:       No risk.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2037    Prevention: No prevention, component test and reviews ensure functionality.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2038  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2039  MD_NvM_8.11_Crc16PtrCast
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2040    Reason: The cast from uint32 to uint16 pointer is necessary to be independent from RAM endiannes: the NvM always needs
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2041            to access the 16 bit CRC value in the first two bytes of the passed uint32 pointer value.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2042    Risk: No risk.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2043    Prevention: No prevention.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2044  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2045  MD_NvM_8.13_NoCrcHandler
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2046    Reason: No Crc handler, used as dummies to avoid differing between CRC and no CRC, has to match the same signature like "real"
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2047          Crc handlers. Because the No Crc handler does nothing, empty functions, the function parameters remain unused and could
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2048          be const -> because of the signature the parameter remains non constant.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2049    Risk: No risk, the functions are empty, they do not use the parameters.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2050    Prevention: No prevention.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2051  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2052  MD_NvM_11.5_CastLossOfConst:
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2053    Reason: Cast removing const qualifier is necessary.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2054    Risk: The component is able to modify the pointer content which could result in undefined behavior.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2055    Prevention: A code review should ensure that the parameters are used correctly.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2056  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2057  MD_NvM_11.5_JobQueue_CastVoidPtrToObjPtr:
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2058    Reason: Cast is necessary to call the job-queue API that is processing the request.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2059    Risk: Cast into an inappropriate type can lead to unexpected behavior.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2060    Prevention: A code review should ensure that the parameters are used correctly.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2061  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2062  MD_NvM_11.5_DataIntegrityJob_CastVoidPtrToObjPtr:
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2063    Reason:     DataIntegrity acts as a proxy to different data integrity mechanisms. They are processed via "jobs" that
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2064                are again represented as a OOP pointer.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2065    Risk:       Wrong job structure could be injected to software submodule. This could lead to wrong memory access.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2066    Prevention: Before usage of each forwarding a certain check is performed to ensure correct job structure usage.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2067  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2068  MD_NvM_13.5:
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2069    Reason: Operands of '&&' or '||' is a helper function that is extracting information and has no side effect.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2070            Usage helps the structure and readability of the code a lot.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2071    Risk: None.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2072    Prevention: None.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2073  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2074  MD_NvM_13.5_ReadAllAndKillReadAll:
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2075    Reason: Finishing the ReadAll request depends on KillReadAll request - if requested the job result shall be
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2076            set to canceled, otherwise the result reflects the result of the finished ReadAll.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2077    Risk: No risk.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2078    Prevention: No prevention, reviews and component test ensure functionality.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2079  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2080  MD_NvM_Dir1.1_CastToVoidPtr:
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2081    Reason: The used callback is defined with a void-pointer to a buffer. As the used buffer type is uint8 there is no
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2082            chance to avoid this cast.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2083    Risk: None. A pointer-to-object can always be converted safely to a pointer-to-void.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2084    Prevention: None.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2085  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2086  MD_NvM_1.1_DataIntegrity_IncompatibleFPtrTypes:
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2087    Reason:     The function pointer of the data integrity module have void pointers for the processed jobs whereas the
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2088                used submodule needs a concrete type.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2089    Risk:       Incompatible pointer could be injected into software submodule, causing disallowed memory access.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2090    Prevention: No prevention, review and component test ensure functionality.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2091  */
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2092  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2093  /***********************************************************************************************************************
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2094   *  SILENTBSW JUSTIFICATIONS
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2095   **********************************************************************************************************************/
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2096  /* SBSW_JUSTIFICATION_BEGIN
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2097  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2098  \ID SBSW_NvM_AccessBlockManagementArea
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2099   \DESCRIPTION Write access to the array storing the NvM block management information about each configured block.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2100                The required array element is accessed via block Id passed to NvM - each block Id is an array index,
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2101                or via internal block Id 0. NvM expects the given block Id to be valid.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2102   \COUNTERMEASURE \R Correctness of given parameter is checked by NvM only in case development mode is enabled.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2103  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2104  \ID SBSW_NvM_Access_CurrBlockInfo
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2105   \DESCRIPTION NvM Write access to NvM internal variable storing information about current block and job. The variable has to be
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2106                initialized correctly by NvM itself.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2107   \COUNTERMEASURE \N The NvM itself is responsible to initialize and access its internal structures correctly. Correct usage is
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2108                   ensured by tests and code reviews.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2109  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2110  \ID SBSW_NvM_PtrAccess_PublicAPI
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2111   \DESCRIPTION Write access to a pointer, which is given to NvM function as parameter. NvM expects the pointer to be valid.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2112   \COUNTERMEASURE \R NvM checks the given pointer not to be NULL before using it, but only in case Development Error Detection is enabled.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2113  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2114  \ID SBSW_NvM_FuncCall_PtrParam_CurrBlockInfo
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2115   \DESCRIPTION NvM passes its current job parameter to internal functions as pointer. There is no explicit check whether the current job is valid,
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2116                the internal function is invoked only during job processing.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2117   \COUNTERMEASURE \N Actions and queries which use the internal job parameter does not check whether the parameter are valid or not. They shall
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2118                   only be invoked in case a valid job is currently running. Correct usage is ensured by tests and code reviews.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2119  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2120  \ID SBSW_NvM_FuncPtrCall_QueryAction
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2121   \DESCRIPTION All accesses to internal queries and actions are done via function pointer calls. There are no explicit checks whether the
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2122                passed function pointer is valid or not, this is ensured via correct implementation.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2123   \COUNTERMEASURE \N The NvM itself is responsible to initialize and access its internal structures correctly. Correct usage is ensured by tests and code reviews.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2124  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2125  \ID SBSW_NvM_FuncCall_PtrParam_ParamChecker
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2126   \DESCRIPTION NvM uses helper functions to check pointer parameter to be valid (development error mode checks). Those functions only check the
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2127                given pointer to be or not to be NULL and return, they do not use the pointer. Functions expects all other parameter to be valid (checked before invoking)
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2128   \COUNTERMEASURE \N Functions are only used to check parameter, not to use them. Their correctness is ensured via component tests and code reviews.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2129  
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2130  \ID SBSW_NvM_FuncCall_PtrParam_FsmQuery
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2131   \DESCRIPTION Within the NvM state machine the next actions to execute are determined via queries. Invoked function gets two function pointers to queries
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2132                stored in an array, checks their results and return accordingly. The function expects a valid parameter to be able to call both queries.
; ..\BSW364\NvM\Implementation\NvM.c	  2133   \COUNTERMEASURE \N The code correctness is ensured via NvM state machine structure and is not tested explicitly. Current tests and
